(Now the third chapter.)
(First section.)
[Section on the examination of the self as distinct from the sense organs (sūtras 1-3)]
3.1.1: Because of the grasping of a single object through sight and touch. {objection sūtra}
3.1.2: No, because of the fixed allocation of [their respective] objects. {objection sūtra}
3.1.3: From that very fixed allocation, because of the existence of the <s>ātman</s> (self) [as the unifying agent] — there is no refutation. {established conclusion sūtra}
