body.translated_text:
3.1.7: Because what is seen by the left [eye] is recognized by the other [eye].
{Established position (<s>siddhānta</s>)}
3.1.8: [Objection:] No, because there is the notion of duality regarding one [entity] separated by the nasal bone.
{Objection (<s>pūrvapakṣa</s>)}
3.1.9: Because when one is destroyed the second is not destroyed, there is no oneness.
{Established position}
3.1.10: [Objection:] This is a groundless [argument], since even when a part is destroyed, the whole is still perceived.
{Objection}
3.1.11: There is no refutation, because of the contradiction with the example.
